   What the records say fits (not changed here): A1's east pocket holds the ruled 4S3P block alone (packfit_west.out);
   A2 is the largest in-case store found with both lid functions kept: base 4S6P (M4a, M5, M6w OPEN) and 39 lid places
   (36 used; a1mech 1 and 2; the check's bound with P2 costing nothing, 43 places); no 21700 lid beats it (SHORTLIST.md 3)

5. THE ENERGY ACCOUNT AND THE SERVICE LEDGER, TYP, 72 h, the 100 W window (Wh over the run; per start; kit and per pack)
   array = the 400 Wp trace at the array; clip = above the window; stage in = into the stage; bus = at VBUS20 before the
   entry's cap (stage and front end losses taken); not taken = refused by the entry's cap or its collapse; U3 = U3's loss;
   node = at the system node; to load = the node's sun used by the load in the hour; accepted = taken into charge at the
   node; spill = offered to charge but refused (packs full or tapering, or the charge ceiling); stored = into the cells;
   chg loss = accepted less stored (U3B, the lid loop, the 0.95 charge efficiency); drawn = out of the cells; lid path =
   the lid's discharge path loss; cut = the first hour each pack stands at its line (the kit's stop puts both there);
   closure = start + stored - drawn - end.
   SERVICE LEDGER (check astra-check-l4e2-1, B1): served = the load in every hour it is carried in full, plus in the stop
   hour the sun and what the stores delivered, nothing in a stopped hour; charge losses = the base's 0.95, U3B and the lid
   loop, the lid's 0.95, and the model's full-store clamp; discharge losses = the lid path, and at the cutoff what the
   stores held but did not deliver; kit residual = node + start - (served + spill + charge losses + discharge losses + end),
   the node summed independently from the chain. The legacy model metric is energy_two_pack's unserved counter, which
   also credits each stopped hour's sun, up to the load, as served while charging with it (the credit printed)
